# "Double all damage equipped creature would deal" (CR 614.1) is about damage FROM the creature the Equipment is attached to,
# and only while it is. Turn 3: Mjölnir is attached to Belladonna Took; Magda, Brazen Outlaw, not equipped, attacks and deals her
# 2 undoubled (Bot2 20 -> 18). Turn 4: Bot2's Llanowar Elves attacks and Belladonna blocks it: the damage dealt TO the equipped
# creature is not doubled (1, not 2: Belladonna survives with 1 damage), while the damage she deals is (4 on a 1/1). Turn 5:
# the Equipment is moved to Magda (Equip worthy {1}), so Magda's damage doubles (4) and Belladonna, equipped no longer, deals her
# plain 2: Bot2 18 -> 12. (Bot1 is at 22: each time Magda attacks and taps she makes a Treasure, and Belladonna gains 1 life for the first token each turn, on turns 3 and 5.) (A second Mjölnir cannot join the first on one creature: it is legendary, CR 704.5j.)

